Id: dbs017f
Severity: FAIL
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Give root a password (ALTER USER 'root'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY ...).
References: mysqld(8)
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-2, IA-5(1); ISO 5.17, 8.5; CE User access control

MySQL lets root in with an empty password: a client connecting
as root with no password is accepted, so anyone reaching the
server has every privilege. This is the one live probe in an
otherwise offline check: it runs only on the running system,
never against an offline root, and reads no credential files.
